{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-parity-regime-selection","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Theorem","doco:Section"],"label":"thm:parity-regime-selection","kind":"theorem","title":"Parity regime selection for Q-values","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-branching-qvalue-factorization","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-confinement-lp"],"tags":["parity","regime-selection","sign","odd-even","q-value","mass-number"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.ParticleInteractions.parity_regime_selection","text":"parity-regime-selection.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"thm:parity-regime-selection\"></a><p>The parity of the mass number <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> fixes the sign of the spectator factor in the <a href=\"#prop:branching-qvalue-factorization\" data-at=\"nuclear-interactions/branching-qvalue\">branching Q-value factorization</a>.</p>\n<h2>Statement</h2>\n<p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">a, b</code> be elements of a strictly ordered field with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">a &#x3C; 0</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b &#x3C; 0</code>, and let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Z, N</code> be natural numbers with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">N \\geq 1</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A = Z + N</code>. Then</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  (-1)^{A-1}\\, a^Z\\, b^{N-1} > 0,</code></pre>\n<p><em>that is, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{sign}(a^Z \\cdot b^{N-1}) = (-1)^{A-1}</code>.</em></p>\n<p>For the per-nucleon channel sums both hypotheses <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">a &#x3C; 0</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b &#x3C; 0</code> hold for all <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q > 1</code> (<a href=\"#def:spectator-normalization\" data-at=\"nuclear-interactions/branching-qvalue\">spectator normalization</a>). How the sign is used to choose a Q-value formula is recorded in the parity-regime dispatch remark below.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/parity-regime-selection.md","heading":"Theorem","number":"14.10.7","page":"b/thm-parity-regime-selection","qa":{"counts":{"pass":64,"fail":1,"warn":1,"na":53,"unknown":0,"stale":109},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Confinement.parity_regime_selection","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Confinement/parity_regime_selection.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
